## The idea

Treat a bad line as **data, not an exception**. Read the input **one line at a time** (never load the whole file), parse each line with `JsonDocument`, and check every field. If anything is wrong, **count it under a reason** and move on. Good lines update a small per-action accumulator: count, sum of latency, max latency and a set of users. The summary is computed from the accumulators at the end, so memory depends on the number of actions and users — not on the size of the file.

## Step by step

1. Consume loops over the lines once with foreach. Blank lines are skipped.
2. TryParse: JsonDocument.Parse inside try/catch → JsonException means NotJson. A root that is not an object → NotAnObject.
3. For "user" and "action": missing → MissingField; not a non-empty string → WrongType. For "ts" and "ms": missing → MissingField; not an integer → WrongType. ms < 0 → OutOfRange.
4. Rejected line → Rejected[reason] += 1. Good line → find or create the accumulator for its action; add to count and sum, update max, add the user to the set; Accepted++.
5. Summary: build one ActionSummary per action (mean = sum / count as a double), then sort by count descending, then action name (ordinal).

## Worked example

**Input:** 4 good lines, then "not json", "[1,2]", one line without ms, one with ts "x", one with ms -1, a blank line

| Step | What happens |
|---|---|
| view u1 100, view u2 300 | view: count 2, sum 400, max 300, users {u1,u2} |
| like u1 50 | like: count 1, sum 50, max 50, users {u1} |
| "not json" / "[1,2]" | NotJson 1 / NotAnObject 1 |
| no "ms" / ts "x" / ms -1 | MissingField 1 / WrongType 1 / OutOfRange 1 |
| blank line | skipped, not counted |
| view u1 200 | view: count 3, sum 600, max 300, users still {u1,u2} |

**Result:** view: 3, mean 200.0, max 300, 2 users; like: 1, mean 50.0 — and 5 rejections, one per reason

## Cost

O(total characters) time, one pass. Memory O(actions + distinct users per action) — the input is never held. Distinct users is the one part that grows with data; at huge scale replace the HashSet with a HyperLogLog sketch.

## The code (C#, compiled and tested against every part of the question)

```csharp
using System.Text.Json;

// One good input line.
public sealed class Event {
    public string User;
    public string Action;
    public long Ts;
    public int Ms;
}

public sealed class Aggregator {
    // Running totals for one action.
    private class Totals {
        public int Count;
        public long SumMs;
        public int MaxMs;
        public HashSet<string> Users = new HashSet<string>();
    }

    private readonly Dictionary<string, Totals> _byAction = new Dictionary<string, Totals>(StringComparer.Ordinal);

    public Dictionary<Reject, int> Rejected { get; } = new Dictionary<Reject, int>();
    public int Accepted { get; private set; }

    // Reads the lines exactly once and keeps only totals — works for a 1 GB file.
    public Aggregator Consume(IEnumerable<string> lines) {
        foreach (string line in lines) {
            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(line)) continue;

            Event e;
            Reject reason;
            if (!TryParse(line, out e, out reason)) {
                int seen;
                Rejected.TryGetValue(reason, out seen);       // 0 if not there yet
                Rejected[reason] = seen + 1;
                continue;                                      // a bad line is data, not a crash
            }

            Totals t;
            if (!_byAction.TryGetValue(e.Action, out t)) {
                t = new Totals();
                _byAction[e.Action] = t;
            }
            t.Count++;
            t.SumMs += e.Ms;
            if (e.Ms > t.MaxMs) t.MaxMs = e.Ms;
            t.Users.Add(e.User);
            Accepted++;
        }
        return this;
    }

    // Sorted by Count descending, then Action ascending (ordinal).
    public IReadOnlyList<ActionSummary> Summary() {
        var result = new List<ActionSummary>();
        foreach (var pair in _byAction) {
            Totals t = pair.Value;
            double mean = (double)t.SumMs / t.Count;           // double: 250 / 2 must be 125.0, not 125
            result.Add(new ActionSummary(pair.Key, t.Count, mean, t.MaxMs, t.Users.Count));
        }
        result.Sort((a, b) => {
            if (a.Count != b.Count) return b.Count.CompareTo(a.Count);   // bigger count first
            return string.CompareOrdinal(a.Action, b.Action);
        });
        return result;
    }

    private static bool TryParse(string line, out Event e, out Reject reason) {
        e = null;
        reason = Reject.NotJson;

        JsonDocument doc;
        try {
            doc = JsonDocument.Parse(line);
        } catch (JsonException) {
            reason = Reject.NotJson;
            return false;
        }

        using (doc) {
            JsonElement root = doc.RootElement;
            if (root.ValueKind != JsonValueKind.Object) {
                reason = Reject.NotAnObject;
                return false;
            }

            string user, action;
            long ts, ms;
            if (!ReadString(root, "user", out user, out reason)) return false;
            if (!ReadString(root, "action", out action, out reason)) return false;
            if (!ReadLong(root, "ts", out ts, out reason)) return false;
            if (!ReadLong(root, "ms", out ms, out reason)) return false;
            if (ms < 0 || ms > int.MaxValue) {
                reason = Reject.OutOfRange;
                return false;
            }

            e = new Event();
            e.User = user;
            e.Action = action;
            e.Ts = ts;
            e.Ms = (int)ms;
            return true;
        }
    }

    private static bool ReadString(JsonElement obj, string name, out string value, out Reject reason) {
        value = null;
        reason = Reject.MissingField;
        JsonElement p;
        if (!obj.TryGetProperty(name, out p)) return false;               // MissingField
        if (p.ValueKind != JsonValueKind.String || string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(p.GetString())) {
            reason = Reject.WrongType;
            return false;
        }
        value = p.GetString();
        return true;
    }

    private static bool ReadLong(JsonElement obj, string name, out long value, out Reject reason) {
        value = 0;
        reason = Reject.MissingField;
        JsonElement p;
        if (!obj.TryGetProperty(name, out p)) return false;               // MissingField
        if (p.ValueKind != JsonValueKind.Number || !p.TryGetInt64(out value)) {
            reason = Reject.WrongType;                                    // a string, or 1.5
            return false;
        }
        return true;
    }
}
```

## Likely follow-up questions

**Q: Missing fields, wrong types, nested objects, an empty file?**

Result type with a reason per line; empty → empty summary

**Q: Time and memory?**

O(lines); O(actions + distinct users)

**Q: What if N is very large?**

Already streaming

**Q: Make it thread-safe / parallel.**

Per-worker accumulators, merge at the end — no shared lock

**Q: The JSON is 1 GB. Can we avoid loading it?**

Line-by-line streaming; for one big array, Utf8JsonReader

**Q: Distinct users at scale.**

HyperLogLog, ~1–2% error

**Q: What do you monitor?**

Reject rate by reason

**Q: Upstream changes the schema.**

Reject spike alert; tolerant reader for additive changes

